{"assets":["/statement-assets/43401299263f07a42fd02b75a7da43382a46aa477e5238fc1d274dc3d4df0bda.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1451","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Circle Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Utkarsh is forced to play yet another one of Ashish's games. The game progresses turn by turn and as usual, Ashish moves "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"first"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the 2D plane. There is a token which is initially at "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$(0,0)$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". In one move a player must increase either the $$$x$$$ coordinate or the $$$y$$$ coordinate of the token by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$k$$$. In doing so, the player must ensure that the token stays within a (Euclidean) distance $$$d$$$ from $$$(0,0)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In other words, if after a move the coordinates of the token are $$$(p,q)$$$, then $$$p^2 + q^2 \\leq d^2$$$ must hold."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The game ends when a player is unable to make a move. It can be shown that the game will end in a finite number of moves. If both players play optimally, determine who will win."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 100$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains two space separated integers $$$d$$$ ($$$1 \\leq d \\leq 10^5$$$) and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\leq k \\leq d$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, if Ashish wins the game, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ashish"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", otherwise print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Utkarsh"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2 1\n5 2\n10 3\n25 4\n15441 33\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nUtkarsh\nAshish\nUtkarsh\nUtkarsh\nAshish\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, one possible sequence of moves can be"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$(0, 0) \\xrightarrow{\\text{Ashish }} (0, 1) \\xrightarrow{\\text{Utkarsh }} (0, 2)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ashish has no moves left, so Utkarsh wins."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/43401299263f07a42fd02b75a7da43382a46aa477e5238fc1d274dc3d4df0bda.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1451D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1451/problem/D"}